{{Life in Balisca}}

'''La Gardunya''' ({{Langx|mxi|لَا غَارْدُونْيَ|La ḡarduńa|the {{W|Beech marten|marten}}}}), known as the '''Baliscan Mafia''' ({{Langx|bl|Mafia Baliscana}}) internationally, is a highly decentralized [[Balisca]]n {{W|criminal society}} and {{W|organized crime}} group. It has been described by some as a coalition of several smaller organizations, rather than a single unified syndicate. These criminal clans have their origins in [[W:Illegalism|illegalist anarchist]] sentiments from all over Balisca: groups in the bigger cities are especially involved in {{W|racketeering}}, [[cybercrime in Balisca|cybercrime/hacking]], money laundering, {{W|weapons trafficking|weapon}} and {{W|drug trafficking}}, while groups in [[Rural society in Balisca|rural Balisca]] are involved [[W:Organopónicos|organopónicos]], [[Social protection in Balisca|social protection]] and [[W:Self-managed social center|self-managed social centers]].

Criminal groups within the Baliscan mainland have also profited from the activities of corrupt officials in [[Abyala]] and [[Kaftia]]. Arms, narcotics and illegal oil are smuggled by Baliscan criminal organizations, often in collaboration with the [[Camorra]] or and other Illypnian groups, from local seaports to important destination centers such as the ports of [[Sanyan]] or [[Volisania]]. Outside of the urban centers, various islands of Balisca, such as [[Sicania]] and [[Piscaria]] are known for having communal-based crime syndicates involved in the trafficking of cocaine on an international level. 

{{W|People smuggling|Migrant smuggling}} and weapon trafficking are activities of choice as well, often collaborating with the [[Siculian Mafia]]. In general, Baliscan organised crime groups are active throughout the [[Northern Hemisphere|Northern]] and [[Western Hemisphere|Western Hemispheres]]. Activity is mainly focused upon the areas of weapons smuggling and the trafficking of marijuana, hashish and cocaine. With Balisca holding a large percentage of the world's [[Ethiopian Ocean|Ethiopic]] maritime merchant shipping, a substantial amount of Baliscan produced drugs are shipped throughout Illypnian on a yearly basis.

At their height, the Gardunya maintained a large presence in Baliscan media and had a larger presence in [[Abyala]]. At their peak in the early 1980s, the [[Autonomous Militia|Autonomous Militias]] estimated that the Gardunya had a membership of more than 80,000. However, this number has drastically dropped, a decline attributed to changing market opportunities and several legal and social developments in Balisca has reversed the growth of membership. There remains no prohibition on Gardunya membership in Balisca today, although many legislative initiatives have been proposed, aiming to impede revenue and increase liability for violent activities.

